3) Competency Question Alignment

**Question:** What is the numeric value of the downstream performance threshold for FTTB and FTTN with AVC TC-4 downstream 25-100 Mbps and upstream 5-40 Mbps?
**Answer:** 50
**Classes:** `Cl_DownstreamPerformanceThreshold`, `AccessTechnology`
**ODP:** Quantities and Units

**Question:** What is the unit of the downstream performance threshold for FTTB and FTTN?
**Answer:** Mbps
**Classes:** `Cl_DownstreamPerformanceThreshold`
**ODP:** Quantities and Units

**Question:** What is the numeric value of the downstream performance threshold for FTTC with AVC TC-4 downstream 50-100 Mbps and upstream 20-40 Mbps?
**Answer:** 50
**Classes:** `Cl_DownstreamPerformanceThreshold`, `AccessTechnology`
**ODP:** Quantities and Units

**Question:** What is the unit of the downstream performance threshold for FTTC?
**Answer:** Mbps
**Classes:** `Cl_DownstreamPerformanceThreshold`
**ODP:** Quantities and Units

**Question:** What is the name of the rebate that applies to Connect Orders for nbn® Ethernet (FTTB), nbn® Ethernet (FTTN), or nbn® Ethernet (FTTC) AVC TC-4 Product Components with bandwidth profiles having a Downstream Performance Threshold?
**Answer:** FTTB/N/C Connection Performance Rebate
**Classes:** `Cl_FTTBNCConnectionPerformanceRebate`
**ODP:** Event

**Question:** What event triggers the applicability of the FTTB/N/C Connection Performance Rebate?
**Answer:** Connect Orders for nbn® Ethernet (FTTB), nbn® Ethernet (FTTN), or nbn® Ethernet (FTTC) AVC TC-4 Product Components with bandwidth profiles for which there is a Downstream Performance Threshold set out in section 15(c)
**Classes:** `Cl_ConnectOrder`, `Cl_FTTBNCConnectionPerformanceRebate`
**ODP:** Event

**Question:** What is the condition under which nbn is not required to pay an FTTB/N/C Connection Performance Rebate because nbn has been unable to obtain at least 7 point-in-time measurements?
**Answer:** nbn has been unable to obtain at least 7 point-in-time measurements of the performance of the relevant AVC TC-4 Ordered Product Component by the Connection Performance Measurement Date
**Classes:** `Cl_FTTBNCConnectionPerformanceRebate`, `Cl_ConnectionPerformanceMeasurementDate`
**ODP:** Event

**Question:** What is the condition under which nbn is not required to pay an FTTB/N/C Connection Performance Rebate because the Information Rate has been reduced, throttled or otherwise constrained?
**Answer:** nbn considers, acting reasonably, that the Information Rate for the relevant AVC TC-4 Ordered Product Component has been reduced, throttled or otherwise constrained other than by nbn
**Classes:** `Cl_FTTBNCConnectionPerformanceRebate`
**ODP:** Event

**Question:** What is the condition under which nbn is not required to pay an FTTB/N/C Connection Performance Rebate because the TC-4 Ordered Product is disconnected by the Connection Performance Measurement Date?
**Answer:** the TC-4 Ordered Product is disconnected by the Connection Performance Measurement Date
**Classes:** `Cl_FTTBNCConnectionPerformanceRebate`, `Cl_ConnectionPerformanceMeasurementDate`
**ODP:** Event

**Question:** What is the condition under which nbn is not required to pay an FTTB/N/C Connection Performance Rebate because the Connect Order is a Service Transfer Order and the RSP is a Related Body Corporate of the Other Losing RSP?
**Answer:** the Connect Order is a Service Transfer Order and the RSP is a Related Body Corporate of the Other Losing RSP
**Classes:** `Cl_ConnectOrder`, `Cl_FTTBNCConnectionPerformanceRebate`
**ODP:** Event

**Question:** What is the condition under which nbn is not required to pay an FTTB/N/C Connection Performance Rebate because the Originally Connected AVC TC-4 has a Downstream Performance Threshold greater than the Connection Assured Rate for the relevant nbn® Copper Pair?
**Answer:** the Originally Connected AVC TC-4 has a Downstream Performance Threshold that is greater than the Connection Assured Rate for the relevant nbn® Copper Pair
**Classes:** `Cl_OriginallyConnectedAVCTC4`, `Cl_DownstreamPerformanceThreshold`, `Cl_ConnectionAssuredRate`, `Cl_nbnCopperPair`
**ODP:** Quantities and Units

**Question:** What type of Connect Orders do FTTB/N/C Connection Performance Rebates not apply to?
**Answer:** Connect Orders which are Transfer Reversals
**Classes:** `Cl_ConnectOrder`, `Cl_FTTBNCConnectionPerformanceRebate`
**ODP:** Event

**Question:** What event must occur before nbn is required to pay an FTTB/N/C Connection Performance Rebate?
**Answer:** nbn has estimated the Measured Connection Rate
**Classes:** `Cl_MeasuredConnectionRate`, `Cl_FTTBNCConnectionPerformanceRebate`
**ODP:** Event

**Question:** How does nbn pay the FTTB/N/C Connection Performance Rebate to the RSP?
**Answer:** by applying it to the RSP Billing Account in accordance with section 8.5.1.5 of the WBA Operations Manual
**Classes:** `Cl_FTTBNCConnectionPerformanceRebate`, `Cl_RSP`
**ODP:** AgentRole

**Question:** What is the name of the rebate offered in respect of nbn® Ethernet (Wireless) Ordered Products supplied using Wireless Network cells that are Persistently Congested?
**Answer:** Wireless Speed Performance Rebate
